Wyreup distributes the library, upstream types and browser source, omitting
the standalone command-line program and its argparse dependency. The library
uses patched dependency ranges, including @xmldom/xmldom 0.9.
Its XML adapter explicitly supplies the XML MIME type and uses the current
onError callback, retaining upstream rejection of parser errors and warnings.
The browser distribution is rebuilt from the verified library source with
the upstream browser replacements. Constituent package versions and complete
license texts appear in vendor/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt and
vendor/BROWSER-DEPENDENCIES.json.
